    "institutions_today": [],
    "paragraph": "\"Deep Learning-Based Road Lane Quality Assessment from Egocentric Dashcam Video\" introduced a baseline framework and a geo-referenced dataset of 63,839 frames from South Texas to automate the evaluation of lane-marking quality. \"Demographics-Informed Neural Network for Multimodal Spatiotemporal Forecasting of Urban Growth and Travel Patterns Using Satellite Imagery\" presented a deep learning framework that uses past image sequences to predict next-year county-level satellite imagery while maintaining demographic consistency. \"Does telehealth narrow the urban-rural gap? A dual assessment of in-person and telehealth prenatal care accessibility\" analyzed 2020–2021 Medicaid claims across 424 South Carolina ZIP Code Tabulation Areas, finding that observed prenatal care utilization was significantly lower in rural areas despite no significant urban-rural difference in predicted in-person accessibility.",
